      <h2>2. What AccountOrbit does</h2>
      <p>AccountOrbit is an independent referral platform. It receives enquiries from people looking for accounting or tax help, reviews them, and may introduce them to a professional where one suitable is available. It also publishes general information.</p>

      <h2>3. What AccountOrbit does not do</h2>
      <p>AccountOrbit does not perform accounting, tax, audit or legal work, and does not give advice for your particular situation. It is not a Chartered Accountant firm, law firm, audit practice, tax authority or government service.</p>

      <h2>4. An introduction is not a promise</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Making an enquiry does not guarantee an introduction, a response within any particular time, or that a professional will accept your work.</li>
        <li>An introduction is not a recommendation that a professional suits your needs, and it is not a statement about their qualifications or quality. Check these yourself before you engage anyone.</li>
        <li>AccountOrbit does not describe any professional as verified or screened. Check credentials at the source, such as {% ext "https://caconnect.icai.org/search-your-ca", "ICAI CA Connect" %}.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>5. Your agreement with a professional</h2>
      <p>If you engage a professional, your contract is with them and not with AccountOrbit. They set the scope, fee and terms with you, and they are responsible for their work. Please get these in writing.</p>

      <h2>6. Fees</h2>
      <p>AccountOrbit does not set professional fees. Ask the professional for their fee in writing before you engage them. {% pending "whether AccountOrbit charges enquirers, and whether professionals pay it." %}</p>

      <h2>7. Your responsibilities</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Give accurate information, and only submit details that you are entitled to share.</li>
        <li>Do not send passwords, OTPs, identity documents or financial records with an enquiry.</li>
        <li>Do not use this site to send spam, misleading enquiries or anything unlawful, or to interfere with how it works.</li>
        <li>You remain responsible for your own tax filings, deadlines and records, even if someone else prepares them.</li>
      </ul>

